From 25127dad7e38048490899e8fdb291f805218ade6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: applejack9050 <applejack9050@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 22:54:54 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] feature: match 16 descriptor rows per block instead of 8

With the dot matrix gone the multiply kernel became limited by re-reading
the second image's descriptors: ncu showed L1/TEX at 86% while DRAM had
fallen to 17%. Each block re-fetches all 128 of its columns' descriptors
for every row-block, so doubling the rows per block halves that traffic.
It also halves the column-partial table that ColMatch_Kernel consumes.

SiftGPU already carried a MULT_BLOCK_DIMY == 16 descriptor-load path for
exactly this shape; only the constant had to change, in both the kernel
and the matcher that sizes the partial tables from it.

RTX 5090 (sm_120), 40 images of south-building, 780 pairs:
  MultiplyDescriptor_Kernel  629us -> 468us  (-26%)
  ColMatch_Kernel            330us -> 132us  (-60%)
  matching GPU total         768ms -> 483ms
  matcher peak GPU memory   952MiB -> 742MiB

The kernel now runs at 96.7% compute and 98.1% L1/TEX throughput, so
this is the end of what retiling buys; registers rise 72 -> 91 and
occupancy drops to 40%, and it is still a clear net win.

Cumulative against the unmodified matcher: GPU time 1166ms -> 483ms
(-59%), peak GPU memory 1762MiB -> 742MiB (-58%).

Match counts remain identical to the original, 201757 over 780 pairs,
on both the plain and the guided path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/thirdparty/SiftGPU/ProgramCU.cu    | 2 +-
 src/thirdparty/SiftGPU/SiftMatchCU.cpp | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/thirdparty/SiftGPU/ProgramCU.cu b/src/thirdparty/SiftGPU/ProgramCU.cu
index 6fdf6a6f..688974e3 100644
--- a/src/thirdparty/SiftGPU/ProgramCU.cu
+++ b/src/thirdparty/SiftGPU/ProgramCU.cu
@@ -1406,7 +1406,7 @@ int ProgramCU::CheckCudaDevice(int device)
 #define MULT_TBLOCK_DIMX 128
 #define MULT_TBLOCK_DIMY 1
 #define MULT_BLOCK_DIMX (MULT_TBLOCK_DIMX)
-#define MULT_BLOCK_DIMY (8 * MULT_TBLOCK_DIMY)
+#define MULT_BLOCK_DIMY (16 * MULT_TBLOCK_DIMY)
 
 // Dot product of two 16-byte descriptor chunks, each held as four 32-bit words
 // packing four unsigned bytes, accumulated into `sum`.
diff --git a/src/thirdparty/SiftGPU/SiftMatchCU.cpp b/src/thirdparty/SiftGPU/SiftMatchCU.cpp
index cbb948cd..9a18a614 100644
--- a/src/thirdparty/SiftGPU/SiftMatchCU.cpp
+++ b/src/thirdparty/SiftGPU/SiftMatchCU.cpp
@@ -42,7 +42,7 @@ using namespace std;
 #define MULT_TBLOCK_DIMX 128
 #define MULT_TBLOCK_DIMY 1
 #define MULT_BLOCK_DIMX (MULT_TBLOCK_DIMX)
-#define MULT_BLOCK_DIMY (8 * MULT_TBLOCK_DIMY)
+#define MULT_BLOCK_DIMY (16 * MULT_TBLOCK_DIMY)
 
 SiftMatchCU::SiftMatchCU(int max_sift) : SiftMatchGPU() {
   _num_sift[0] = _num_sift[1] = 0;
